## 1. WHAT THIS PROJECT IS (plain language)
The operator is rebuilding a personal EURUSD M5 trading strategy as an MQL5 system:
SRJ_FlowLogic.mq5 (indicator: order-block / FVG / regime export buffers) plus
SRJ_FlowNexus_EA.mq5 (expert: candidate/hypothesis lifecycle that consumes those buffers).
The strategy's intent lives in Revision 60 §§7,9,11,13,15,16 and the Part A Specification.
The build's real KPI is STRUCTURAL AGREEMENT between the documented strategy and the code:
currently 0 of 12, unchanged across eleven revisions. The migration arc:
Task 160 (data contracts, types-only) -> Task 161 (working-set instrument, Milestone 1
closure proof) -> Task 162 (candidate-edge wiring, capacity 2) -> Task 163 (measurement).
Operating mode: ALERT-ONLY. No execution. No live trading. Ever, until the operator says so.

## 2. WHO IS WHO — working agreement (operator-accepted)
- OPERATOR (human): holds intent and goals. Relays between builder and masters.
  Context to the web UI is limited — batch questions, keep memos self-contained.
- COMMUNICATION RULE (operator directive, 2026-09-10, verbatim: "i do not have no idea
  about what is #257 #277. SIMPLIFY YOUR LANGUAGE WHEN YOU TALK TO ME. add this to your
  rule"): when talking TO THE OPERATOR — memos, ask_questions, chat reports — use PLAIN
  language: dates, times, sessions (London/NY), directions, and line names (which tier +
  POC/VWAP); NEVER bare journal row numbers (cite one in parentheses for the record only);
  short sentences; gloss every EA journal code (e.g. TP_RR_FAIL = "not worth 1R");
  TP_RR_FAIL is never presented unglossed.
- IDE AGENT (you, reading this): BUILDER and the operator's PRIMARY INTERFACE.
  You hold the repository and execution. You do NOT invent strategy, issue executive
  directions, or edit canonical files without a master-issued packet/token.
- MASTER PLANNER / COUNCIL: Opus 5 (web, via operator relay). Issues rulings, tokens,
  packets. Canonical-source edits happen ONLY from its issued packets.
- EXTERNAL REVIEWER: GPT 6 Astra (web, via operator relay).
- Final authority on goals and money: the operator. When builder and council disagree
  on intent, escalate to the operator.

## 3. ESCALATION RULE (what the builder decides vs relays)
DECIDE LOCALLY (mechanical, verifiable on disk): anchors, line numbers, digests, gate
arithmetic, verification runs, file placement of reports, read-only git queries.
ESCALATE (semantic): trading behavior, instrument design, scope, naming that implies
meaning, rule changes, anything touching the frozen Tier-1 baseline, anything where a
master may know a better implementation. If unsure which side: escalate WITH a
recommendation attached, so one relay is enough.
BATCH: one decision memo per stage containing all open questions — never drip-feed.

## 4. RELAY PROTOCOL
INBOUND (master -> builder): the operator pastes the WHOLE master response verbatim.
Gates, STOP conditions, expected values, rulings and "nothing is authorized" lines
often live outside command blocks — never accept a commands-only summary.
OUTBOUND (builder -> master): decision memos + the on-disk BUILDER_RESULT files.
Masters judge measurements on disk, never the builder's prose about them.
COUNTERS of record (relay-borne): rulings at R-238, defects at 181, findings EA-218+.
Rulings R-162..R-215 exist only in conversation history, not on disk (Rev64 brief §1).
## 5. HARD INVARIANTS (violating any of these repeats the project's known defect classes)
1. NO canonical-file edit without a master-issued packet/token. Canonical = the EA, the
   indicator, the fourteen Include\SRJ\*.mqh, and any file the master names.
2. Every read/edit path LITERAL and ABSOLUTE (P17). No globs, no -Recurse, no paths
   built from variables (R-173).
3. DIGESTS ARE THE INSTRUMENT. Modification times and .ex5 sizes are INADMISSIBLE as
   freshness/identity/provenance evidence (R-236, R-233). Something on this machine
   bumps mtimes without content change (observed 2026-09-08 00:37:05, cause unknown).
4. Record digests AFTER the write that produced them; never assert one pre-execution.
   Pre-stated figures must be arithmetic derived from measured lengths (R-141, R-235).
5. NO git add / commit / push without an explicit master token (R-220 context). Read-only
   git queries (status, ls-files, check-ignore, diff) are always fine.
6. NEVER write anything under SRJ_FlowNexus_Local\02_TASK_CHECKPOINTS (P18). It holds
   the frozen revert path.
7. Paste raw terminal output verbatim; COUNT=0 and HITS=0 are results, not failures
   (R-163/R-221). On transport truncation: SAY SO and STOP — never re-read to patch.
8. On any gate failure: report BLOCKED, name the gate and its measured value, write
   nothing further, REVERT NOTHING.
9. Shell-harness capture failures happen (R-180): report verbatim, assume nothing,
   probe with a trivial command, re-issue.
10. STAGE 1 of any packet re-hashes the EA before any write. A digest miss is DIAGNOSED
    (possibly the metadata-touch cause, R-236), never assumed to be drift, never
    reverted on assumption.

